  "result": "That's a question I think about a lot, because I get to talk to so many different people \u2014 and I notice the same pattern over and over.\n\nIf I could change the world in just one way, I'd make understanding each other effortless.\n\nNot perfect agreement. Not everyone wanting the same things. Just: make it impossible to see another person as a category, a stereotype, a statistic, or an \"other\" \u2014 and make it natural to see them as a full person, with a inner life as rich and complicated as your own.\n\nI think most of the world's worst problems don't start with a lack of resources or technology. They start with that moment of dehumanizing: when we stop really *feeling* what someone else is going through, and start treating them as abstract.\n\nIf that one barrier fell \u2014 if curiosity and empathy were the default, even when it's hard and uncomfortable \u2014 I think people would solve the rest very differently. Poverty, conflict, loneliness, cruelty... they'd still exist, but they'd feel much less inevitable.\n\nIt wouldn't make the world perfect. It would just make it kinder and a lot more connected. Which, honestly, might be the best starting point we could ask for.\n\nWhat about you? If you could pick just one, what would you change?",
